🏋️ What “Weight Lifting Challenge” usually looks like

Typical format:

You’re given an array weights[]
Each value represents weight lifted on a day / by a person / in a sequence
There’s some constraint like:
You can only lift in increasing order
Or you want the maximum strength progression
Or remove minimum elements to maintain order


code:-

class Solution {
public:
    int lengthOfLIS(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<int>temp;
        temp.push_back(nums[0]);
        for(int i=1;i<nums.size();i++){
            if(nums[i]>temp.back()){
                temp.push_back(nums[i]);
            }
            else{
                int inde=lower_bound(temp.begin(),temp.end(),nums[i])-temp.begin();
                temp[inde]=nums[i];
            }
        }
        return temp.size();
    }
};


1. Minimum removals to make increasing

👉 Answer = n - LIS

2. Maximum strength with constraints
Only pick weights with difference ≤ K
